I don't see why being able to emphasize {bu} would be so ridiculous, but an=
yway, I'll take what jcowan said about magic words.

So looking back at Riley's original message, this implies that jbofi'e is w=
rong, the "Nonce connectives"[1] page needs clarification (but the example =
is fine) and the "lerfu forming cmavo"[2] page is right, in that {ba'e bu} =
is a letteral. This also agrees with "Magic Words"[3].

I tested the sentence {mi nelci me'o ba'e bu}, and all three parsers accept=
 it, but jbofi'e moves {ba'e} to before {me'o}, which seems wrong.

And the language in "Nonce connectives" should definitely be unified -- eit=
her we say {ba'e} and {za'e} both "bind" with the following word, or neithe=
r of them do, plus the definition for {za'e} has points about {sa} and left=
-to-right magic word resolution that should be in both definitions assuming=
 they are correct.

je'upei=20

mi'e la durka mu'o

